00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.789 align:start position:0%
french police officers patrol a beach at  night near calais  on a mission to prevent migrants and  refugees from trying to cross the  english channel to reach the uk  by boat they've crossed the  mediterranean and survived many dangers  so when they arrive here and see the  last 30 or so kilometers it seems like  nothing  people smugglers charge migrants  thousands of dollars for a place on a  boat  they often use old bunkers like this one  to hide material  we've found boats and life jackets here  in the past what happens is the migrants  wait in the dunes over there the  smugglers retrieve their material  and they all go out to sea there were  nearly ten thousand  attempted crossings last year at least  six people  died police have bolstered security  along the coast  and britain's helping to fund patrols  that now take place around the clock  with some officers on motorbikes  it's a recent phenomenon that's been on  the rise since 2019 because security has  been tightened on  ferries and in the ports it's much  harder to reach the uk by classic means  so migrants are now trying their luck on  inflatable boats  from here you can just about see the  british coastline through the haze it is  less than 40 kilometers away and for the  migrants and refugees that are trying to  cross the english channel  their goal isn't necessarily to reach  the land but to enter uk waters about  halfway because at that point they have  effectively reached britain  many of the migrants are from eritrea  sudan  iraq or afghanistan stuck in squalid  conditions in calais some say that the  police harassed them  we saw officers clear hundreds of people  from a camp  this group of young afghans say that  they'll risk a boat crossing  for a decent life most say they have  friends or family  in england i have one friend who made it  by sea  we have to take a risk by boat scared or  not there's no choice we have to make it  i don't care about the risk because i  left danger in afghanistan  and now it's dangerous to stay here  brexit and the pandemic haven't  dissuaded  some from trying to reach britain or  ended dreams of the sort of safety that  many take for granted  so some people continue to risk their  life for opportunities they believe  lie on the horizon natasha butler al  jazeera  kelly
 

